# q083 customer_by_segment_crawl — browse-parity E1 (D7). A property-scoped
#   "listing" crawl: a variable subject bound by a PROPERTY (edw:segment, object
#   var) rather than a class, limit 10. At 733cb2c8e this DNF'd (>90s): the LIMIT
#   row budget was not forwarded to the property-var crawl's full-source wildcard
#   scan (it ran as the unbudgeted inner scan). E1 estimates that pruning-key-less
#   wildcard as a full-source scan so reorder makes it the LIMIT-budgeted
#   correlated OUTER, driven by the selective edw:segment scan — so it terminates.
#   RowsOnly: the LIMIT truncates the unordered set.
{
  "@context": {"edw": "http://ns.fluree.dev/edw#"},
  "select": {"?s": ["*"]},
  "where": {"@id": "?s", "edw:segment": "?v"},
  "limit": 10
}
